{
  "_about": [
    "Golden cases for the edit lane frame and for the rules that decide whether an edit may be sent and whether a received one applies.",
    "Normative: docs/sealed-messages.md §Edits.",
    "The editor is never in the payload: it is the MLS sender. Parsing is strict JSON, as for deletes; `n` MUST be a JSON integer from 1 to 10, and `b` MUST NOT be blank after trimming.",
    "`decide` cases answer `apply`, `drop` or `wait`. An empty `sender` drops. The author check is the delete's (delete.json, `honor`): with a `record` the sender must equal it; with none, `author` (the author the device otherwise knows for the row, or \"\") stands in; with neither the edit waits. A sender who is not the author drops.",
    "Then: a withdrawn target (`deleted`) drops; an edit received more than 48 hours after the target (`editAtMs - targetAtMs > 172800000`) drops, and exactly 48 hours is still in; `revision` (`n`) must be above `current`, the revision already applied (0 for an unedited message), or it drops. Otherwise it applies.",
    "`canSend` cases pin when Edit is offered: the sender's own message, not withdrawn, at most 24 hours old (`nowMs - targetAtMs <= 86400000`), and edited fewer than 10 times.",
    "`pending` cases pin waiting edits, kept per (message id, sender) with only the highest `n` per sender. When the target is attributable every kept sender is judged with `decide`, the author's edit is returned if it applies, and every entry for that id is forgotten. A `target` step's `expect` is the applied edit {n, body} or null; `pending` is what is left: message id to sorted senders.",
    "To replay: run each case through your own implementation of the format and compare the result with the case's expectation, field by field."
  ],
